hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3046","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Rafi’, narrated to us Yahya—meaning ibn Adam—narrated to us Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, regarding a man who swears by walking to the Ka’bah but then becomes unable to do so and rides instead.\n\nIbn ‘Abbas (RA) said: \He may ride next year as much as he wishes"","" walk as much as he wishes"","" and ride.\""\n\nSharik said: Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman"","" the freed slave of Abu Talhah"","" narrated to us from Kurayb"","" from Ibn ‘Abbas (RA)"","" who elevated it to the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \""He may ride and expiate his oath.\"""""""
"3047","Narrated to us Abu 'Ammar, narrated to us Al-Fadl ibn Musa, from Shariq, from Muhammad, the freed slave of Abu Talhah, from Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas (RA) that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said:\n\n\Indeed"","" my sister has vowed to walk to the House (the Ka'bah).\"" So he (ﷺ) said: \""Allah does not require the hardship of your sister in any way. Tell her to perform Hajj riding and to expiate her oath.\""\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
